  "plain": "A guest on Jesse Michels's podcast shows an article he wrote about remote viewing, the attempt to see faraway places using only the mind. He says it covers two 1970s government programmes, Stargate and Scanate, run with the DIA, the US military's intelligence agency, and the CIA, America's foreign spy agency, with work done by the physicists Hal Puthoff and Russell Targ at the Stanford Research Institute in California. As told, it shows the government took psychic spying seriously enough to pay for it."
